# Email Triage Agent — environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your own values.
# Never commit your real `.env` to git.
#
# The agent itself does not read this file. Inbox addresses and
# tool commands are set in .claude/agents/email-triage.md (see
# "Customising" in the README). This file is for the credentials
# that YOUR email CLI and PMS scripts need, if they load a `.env`.

# ============================================================
# PMS (Property Management System) credentials
# ============================================================
# Only needed if your lookup / notes scripts read them from here.
# The names below are the Cloudbeds reference setup; use whatever
# names your own scripts expect.

# CLOUDBEDS_CLIENT_ID=""
# CLOUDBEDS_CLIENT_SECRET=""
# CLOUDBEDS_ACCESS_TOKEN=""
# CLOUDBEDS_REFRESH_TOKEN=""

# ============================================================
# Email provider credentials
# ============================================================
# Most email CLIs keep their own login (for example an OAuth
# login stored by the CLI). Add variables here only if your
# wrapper asks for them.
